2709.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T01:17:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133982790,imgsize-75652.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Officer asked to show Outlook or Teams as evidence of working: OPT student shares domestic travel experience to New Mexico]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133981977.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/officer-asked-to-show-outlook-or-teams-as-evidence-of-working-opt-student-shares-domestic-travel-experience-to-new-mexico/articleshow/133981977.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/officer-asked-to-show-outlook-or-teams-as-evidence-of-working-opt-student-shares-domestic-travel-experience-to-new-mexico/articleshow/133981977.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T00:52:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133982271,imgsize-125650.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chen Ziyi Death Details: Mukbang star dies at 24 after health warning; raises concern over extreme eating]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133981416.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chen Ziyi, known online as Ganfan Yingying, was a 24-year-old Chinese mukbang creator with about 1.2 million followers. She died on August 17, 2026, days after revealing that her potassium level had dropped to 2.3 mmol/L. Chen had spoken about purging after extreme eating sessions. Her parents confirmed her death but did not disclose an official cause.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/chen-ziyi-cause-of-death-what-happened-to-chinese-mukbang-streamer-who-died-at-24/articleshow/133981416.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/chen-ziyi-cause-of-death-what-happened-to-chinese-mukbang-streamer-who-died-at-24/articleshow/133981416.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T00:31:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sumit Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133981416,imgsize-49085.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dan Houser Net Worth In 2026: Rockstar co-founder hits $250m; GTA success fuels fortune]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133980961.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Dan Houser, a co-founder of Rockstar Games, built an impressive $250 million fortune thanks to the immense popularity of games like Grand Theft Auto, which he helped create. After two decades of leading the studio's creative vision, he departed in 2020. His significant investments in real estate highlight his financial success, and with the anticipated launch of Grand Theft Auto 6, additional revenue is expected to flow in.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/esports/news/dan-houser-net-worth-in-2026-how-rich-is-the-rockstar-games-co-founder/articleshow/133980961.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/esports/news/dan-houser-net-worth-in-2026-how-rich-is-the-rockstar-games-co-founder/articleshow/133980961.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T00:20:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133981269,imgsize-749044.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2012, an English upland restoration project began fencing sheep out of Tebay Common]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133938757.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A transformative upland restoration initiative in Cumbria has brought new life to a sheep-grazed fell, with native trees being planted to stimulate the recovery of dormant seed banks and form enchanting ghost woodlands. This environmental project has witnessed the arrival of eleven new breeding bird species since 2016. Additionally, it enhances natural flood management and boosts local farming incomes through sustainable environmental agreements supporting upland livestock.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2012-an-english-upland-restoration-project-began-fencing-sheep-out-of-tebay-common-60000-trees-later-lost-woodland-is-returning-and-11-new-breeding-bird-species-have-been-recorded-since-2016/articleshow/133938757.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2012-an-english-upland-restoration-project-began-fencing-sheep-out-of-tebay-common-60000-trees-later-lost-woodland-is-returning-and-11-new-breeding-bird-species-have-been-recorded-since-2016/articleshow/133938757.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T04:43:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133940222,imgsize-819741.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1864, Tasmania introduced brown trout from England for sport; 162 years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133937498.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Conservation workers are building barriers and clearing waterways to save native Swan galaxias.  This tiny fish faces extinction after brown trout were introduced over 160 years ago.  Natural barriers helped some populations survive, but droughts and floods pose risks.  Teams are creating trout-free refuges and moving fish to safe, isolated catchments.  These efforts balance angling tradition with crucial species recovery for native wildlife.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-1864-tasmania-introduced-brown-trout-from-england-for-sport-162-years-later-conservationists-are-creating-trout-free-havens-for-a-native-fish-with-only-about-6000-left/articleshow/133937498.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-1864-tasmania-introduced-brown-trout-from-england-for-sport-162-years-later-conservationists-are-creating-trout-free-havens-for-a-native-fish-with-only-about-6000-left/articleshow/133937498.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T03:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133938673,imgsize-1585695.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Couple Cut LA Home Price: Sarah Michelle Gellar and Freddie Prinze Jr. trim ask; $9.95m tag after $550k cut]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133951389.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Sarah Michelle Gellar and Freddie Prinze Jr. have decided to drop the price of their Mandeville Canyon home, now listed at $9.95 million. This price cut comes only three months after the property was first put on the market. The couple bought this family residence in 2013 and is now eager to find a buyer for their beloved Los Angeles home.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2013-sarah-michelle-gellar-and-freddie-prinze-jr-paid-6-1-million-for-their-la-home-13-years-later-they-have-cut-the-asking-price-to-9-95-million/articleshow/133951389.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2013-sarah-michelle-gellar-and-freddie-prinze-jr-paid-6-1-million-for-their-la-home-13-years-later-they-have-cut-the-asking-price-to-9-95-million/articleshow/133951389.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T02:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133951443,imgsize-1308179.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trash Talk Nyc Project: 100-day cleanup sparks gardens; neighbours build a movement]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133950491.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[David Clarke took it upon himself to clean a neglected block in New York City using simple tools. His shared updates on social media sparked wider community interest, leading to a collaborative effort. He invested his own funds to create gardens in tree beds, inspiring neighbors to participate in maintaining the area. This grassroots initiative revitalized the block and fostered a sense of community pride in public spaces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-yorker-cleaned-the-same-washington-heights-block-every-day-for-100-days-and-spent-2000-on-it-then-his-neighbours-joined-in/articleshow/133950491.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-yorker-cleaned-the-same-washington-heights-block-every-day-for-100-days-and-spent-2000-on-it-then-his-neighbours-joined-in/articleshow/133950491.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T02:47:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133950532,imgsize-1106383.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[18-year-old wins scholarship after first flight sparks aviation dream]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0"